<p>President Trump approved a joint U.S.-Israeli operation against Iran after a phone call in which Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu urged him to target Supreme Leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei, according to source-based reporting cited across the four articles. Reuters-based accounts say the call took place less than 48 hours before the strike began, making it a pivotal moment in the lead-up to the operation.</p><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Shared intelligence: Reuters-based reporting says Trump and Netanyahu had both been briefed earlier in the week before they spoke, giving them a shared factual basis for the discussion.</li><li>Call as catalyst: The Straits Times says Netanyahu&#x27;s phone appeal helped push Trump toward approving the operation.</li><li>Israeli urgency: NDTV says Netanyahu was determined to move ahead when he made the case to Trump.</li><li>Leadership concentration: SCMP says the expected opening depended on Khamenei and key lieutenants being at his compound in Tehran at the same time.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Benjamin Netanyahu: According to the reports, Netanyahu added a personal-retaliation argument to his pitch, saying a strike could avenge earlier Iranian efforts to assassinate Trump. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/iran-war-news-inside-the-call-between-trump-netanyahu-that-sealed-ali-khameneis-fate-11257417#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li><li>President Trump: Reuters-based reporting portrays Trump as being asked to join the kind of complex, distant war he once campaigned against, underscoring the political reversal in the decision. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/exclusive-trump-approved-iran-operation-after-netanyahu-argued-joint-killing'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>Reuters-sourced officials: Unnamed sources in the Reuters-based stories framed the moment as a chance to strike Iran&#x27;s top leadership echelon at once, which is why the articles describe it as a potential decapitation strike. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3347640/trump-approved-iran-operation-after-netanyahu-argued-joint-killing-khamenei'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/iran-war-news-inside-the-call-between-trump-netanyahu-that-sealed-ali-khameneis-fate-11257417#publisher=newsstand'>Inside Trump-Netanyahu Call 48 Hours Before Khamenei&#x27;s Killing In Iran War</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/exclusive-trump-approved-iran-operation-after-netanyahu-argued-joint-killing'>Exclusive-Trump approved Iran operation after Netanyahu argued for joint killing of Khamenei, sources say</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3347640/trump-approved-iran-operation-after-netanyahu-argued-joint-killing-khamenei'>Trump approved Iran operation ‘after Netanyahu argued for joint killing of Khamenei’</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/trump-approved-iran-operation-after-netanyahu-argued-for-joint-killing-of-khamenei-sources-say'>Trump approved Iran operation after Netanyahu argued for joint killing of Khamenei, sources say</a> - straitstimes.com</li></ul>